Subject: [PATCH] sched/cpufreq: rename schedutil to dynasched

Rename the schedutil governor's exposed name to "dynasched" so the
on-device runtime tuner shipped with this kernel can detect a Tensor
G3-tuned build without colliding with stock schedutil on non-rooted
boots. The actual tuning logic (per-cluster rate-limits, governor
re-application on screen state changes, etc.) lives in
success-metadata/pixel8-runtime-tuner-<variant>.sh.

Signed-off-by: deepongi-labs
---
 kernel/sched/cpufreq_schedutil.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/cpufreq_schedutil.c b/kernel/sched/cpufreq_schedutil.c
--- a/kernel/sched/cpufreq_schedutil.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/cpufreq_schedutil.c
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 struct cpufreq_governor schedutil_gov = {
-	.name			= "schedutil",
+	.name			= "dynasched",
 	.owner			= THIS_MODULE,
 	.flags			= CPUFREQ_GOV_DYNAMIC_SWITCHING,
 	.init			= sugov_init,
